From a24ed4c45392aa36660692403f2ab6052e579136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:45:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): a touch probe section starts no spindle on any
 mill post

Haas, Tormach, Sinumerik, Heidenhain and Mazak posted "S<rpm> M3" (or
MOTON) for every section, a probe's S0 included. Each now gates its
spindle start on sRpm > 0, the rule fanuc.cps has used since #108.
Tools refuse rpm 0, so only a probe reaches it; every post's section-end
M5 already leaves the spindle stopped for the next section.

Pinned by probe_spindle::{a_section_with_no_spindle_speed_starts_no_spindle_on_any_mill_post,
a_cutting_section_still_starts_its_spindle_on_every_mill_post}.

Fixes #523

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
